WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.889 --> 00:00:06.680
14 Actors You May Not Know Are Dead

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:11.920
When we watch celebrities at the movies or
on TV, we develop special bonds with them.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:17.890
So when they're gone too soon, it can be devastating – especially
when we don't realize we've lost them. You

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:22.689
may not know some of these actors by name,
but you certainly know their faces. Some of

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:27.019
your favorite movies or shows feature actors
that have been taken from the world well before

00:00:27.019 --> 00:00:28.210
their time.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.769
Lee Thompson Young

00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:34.640
The Famous Jett Jackson, Lee Thompson Young's
star vehicle, was a very popular show on The

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.359
Disney Channel for some time. Friday Night
Lights, Akeelah and the Bee, and The Hills

00:00:39.359 --> 00:00:44.379
Have Eyes II are some of the few films on
Young's impressive resume. But while working

00:00:44.379 --> 00:00:49.960
as a series regular on Rizzoli and Isles,
he was diagnosed with Bipolar Disorder. Sadly,

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:56.690
on August 19, 2013, his life came to a tragic
end after he committed suicide with a self-inflicted

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:58.190
gunshot wound.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:59.589
Brittany Murphy

00:00:59.589 --> 00:01:04.960
After rising to fame in 1995's cult classic
Clueless with the famous line "You're a virgin

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:10.350
who can't drive," Brittany Murphy offered
strong performances in Girl Interrupted, Drop

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:16.090
Dead Gorgeous, 8 Mile, and Sin City, and had
a regular role on the hit animated show King

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:20.430
of the Hill. Murphy was the breadwinner of
the family, as she cared for her mother, a

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:25.180
breast-cancer survivor, and her husband, Simon
Monjack, who suffered from frequent seizures

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:29.740
and heart troubles. In a surprising turn of
events that shocked the world, Murphy was

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:37.130
declared dead on December 20, 2009, due to
pneumonia, anemia, and multiple drug intoxication.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:42.719
It's unclear whether toxic mold also played
a part in her untimely death at age 32, as

00:01:42.719 --> 00:01:46.869
her husband was found dead in the same house
five months later.

00:01:46.869 --> 00:01:48.329
Heather O'Rourke

00:01:48.329 --> 00:01:52.310
Best known for playing Carol Anne from the
movie Poltergeist, Heather O'Rourke was the

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:57.340
sweet young girl that terrified audiences
after being sucked into the television set.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.280
She was also one of a very small number of
original cast members that remained with the

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:06.460
movie series until Poltergeist 3. If you've
seen the final movie, you will notice Heather's

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:11.450
cheeks are very puffy — a reaction to the
medication she was taking for Crohn's disease,

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:16.390
with which she was misdiagnosed. Tragedy struck
when Heather suffered from cardiac arrest

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:21.849
in February 1988 while undergoing a surgery
for a bowel obstruction at the tender age

00:02:21.849 --> 00:02:23.310
of 12.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:23.800
Dominique Dunne

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:29.970
Sadly, this is another actress from the 1982
film Poltergeist. Many say the film was cursed,

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:34.629
as this young actress from the film also met
an early demise. Dominique was born into a

00:02:34.629 --> 00:02:39.730
life of privilege in Santa Monica to a ranching
heiress and TV writer and producer Dominick

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:45.310
Dunne. Dominique made appearances in the TV
shows Chips, Fame, and The Quest. But the

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:50.519
same year Poltergeist was released, her deranged
ex-boyfriend, John Thomas Sweeney, murdered

00:02:50.519 --> 00:02:56.190
her in her own driveway in West Hollywood
on November 4, 1982.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:57.340
Brad Renfro

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:02.450
Skyrocketing to fame at age 11, Brad Renfro
made a huge impression on audiences after

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:07.890
starring in Joel Schumacher's adaptation of
The Client by John Grisham. High profile roles

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:12.650
followed, and he made appearances in Sleepers
opposite Brad Pitt, Ghost World alongside

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:18.170
Scarlett Johansson, and The Informers starring
Kim Basinger. Renfro fulfilled the sad destiny

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:24.430
of many child actors, plunging into a life
of illegal drug use and trouble with the law.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:29.530
After trying to buy drugs from an undercover
LA police officer in 2006, Renfro plead no

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:35.239
contest to attempted possession of heroin
and spent ten days in jail. On January 15,

00:03:35.239 --> 00:03:41.019
2008, at 25 years old, Brad Renfro was found
dead of an accidental heroin and morphine

00:03:41.019 --> 00:03:42.220
overdose.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.290
Jonathan Brandis

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:48.580
With a resume as long as your arm, Jonathan
Brandis showed up in Who's the Boss?, Blossom,

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:54.680
L.A. Law, Full House, The Wonder Years, and
Murder, She Wrote, among tons of others. As

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:59.799
a child and teenage star for many years, it
seemed like he had no shortage of work. He

00:03:59.799 --> 00:04:05.379
was 16 when he made Ladybugs, and 17 when
he was cast as a teen genius in Steven Spielberg's

00:04:05.379 --> 00:04:11.439
SeaQuest 2032. When SeaQuest was canceled
in 1996, however, the once-plentiful casting

00:04:11.439 --> 00:04:16.959
offers dried up. Depression soon plagued the
young star. He died after sustaining injuries

00:04:16.959 --> 00:04:22.360
from an attempted suicide via hanging at the
age of 27 in Danbury, Connecticut.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:23.830
Dana Plato

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:28.550
Playing Kimberly Drummond in the television
series Diff'rent Strokes, Dana Plato was catapulted

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:33.650
to instant stardom alongside Gary Coleman
and Todd Bridges. To cope with the mounting

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:39.100
pressures of fame, she often indulged in cocaine
and marijuana off-set. Once she became pregnant,

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:43.570
however, the network released her from her
contract and she began a downward spiral of

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:49.240
drugs and alcohol that included work in adult
films and a spread in Playboy magazine. Dana

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:54.800
moved to Las Vegas where, desperate for cash,
she robbed a store for less than $200 and

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:59.910
was bonded out of jail by Vegas entertainer
Wayne Newton. She died at the age of 35 on

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:07.220
May 8, 1999, in her RV in Oklahoma after taking
a fatal dose of lortab and valium.

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.670
Lisa Robin Kelly

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:13.490
Kelly made audiences laugh as part of the
ensemble cast of That '70s Show, but her real

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:18.040
life wasn't funny at all. After a lengthy
battle with drug and alcohol addiction that

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:24.270
ultimately caused her to lose her job on the
show, Kelly checked into rehab in August 2013,

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:29.450
only to pass away in her sleep due to complications
from an accidental overdose. She was only

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:30.390
43.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:31.960
Thuy Trang

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:36.880
Best known for her work as the original Yellow
Ranger on Mighty Morphin Power Rangers, Thuy

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:41.080
Trang was developing what seemed like a potentially
promising career after leaving the show in

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:47.660
1994, landing roles in Spy Hard and The Crow:
City of Angels. Sadly, she never had a chance

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:54.290
to fulfill that potential — she was killed
in a car accident in 2001, at the age of 27.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.200
Michael Clarke Duncan

00:05:56.200 --> 00:06:00.800
Duncan's towering physique made him a natural
for "big guy" roles, but he really had dramatic

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:05.340
chops — and unlike a lot of actors booked
for that type of part, he got a chance to

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:10.930
show them. His too-brief filmography includes
memorable supporting turns in Armageddon and

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:15.740
Daredevil, as well as a beautifully sensitive
starring performance in the big-screen adaptation

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:20.700
of Stephen King's The Green Mile. Duncan should
have had a much longer career, but he was

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:25.040
felled by a heart attack in 2012 at the age
of 54.

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:26.090
Harold Ramis

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:30.670
Known best for playing the role of Egon in
Ghostbusters, Harold Ramis brought his screenwriting

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:36.310
and directing talents to a slew of some of
Hollywood's best-loved films, including Caddyshack,

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:41.590
Animal House, and Groundhog Day, just to name
a few. Ramis was 70 when he passed away from

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:47.900
an autoimmune disease in 2014. Though he enjoyed
a long and productive career, fans the world

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:51.340
over know he was still taken far too soon.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:52.410
Andy Hallett

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:57.800
A Buffyverse fan favorite for his work as
the demon Lorne in the spinoff series Angel,

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:02.740
Andy Hallett seemed to be on the verge of
a fruitful career in Hollywood. Unfortunately,

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:08.910
he passed away at the age of 33 in 2009, the
victim of congestive heart failure.

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:10.130
Taylor Negron

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:15.250
One of Hollywood's all-time ultimate "That
Guy" actors, Negron compiled an impressive

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:19.950
list of memorable credits without ever becoming
a household name in his own right. Although

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:24.550
he tended to be on screen for no more than
a few moments at a time, Negron's deadpan

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:29.860
delivery made him a standout in pictures like
Fast Times at Ridgemont High and Better Off

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:35.930
Dead, as well as TV shows like Seinfeld and
Friends. He was only 57 when he died in early

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:39.550
2015, a victim of liver cancer.

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:43.610
"Rowdy" Roddy Piper
After making a name for himself as a professional

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:48.630
wrestler, Piper branched out onto the big
screen, where he starred in the 1988 cult

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:54.050
classic They Live. He's the one who coined
the catchphrase, "I have come here to chew

00:07:54.050 --> 00:08:03.750
bubble gum and kick ass. And I'm all out of
bubble gum." That set the tone for a busy

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:08.560
Hollywood career full of B-movie roles and
small, but unforgettable appearances on shows

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:14.440
like It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia. He
died in his sleep in 2015 after suffering

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:18.650
a pulmonary embolism that triggered a heart
attack at the age of 61.

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:22.650
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to see more videos like the one you

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:27.090
just saw. And leave us a comment to tell us
your favorite memories of celebs who left

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:27.690
us too soon.

